<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marcus Fulvius Nobilior</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 193–179 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marcus Fulvius Nobilior was a Roman general and consul in 189 BCE. As praetor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania-ulterior">Hispania Ulterior</a> he defeated the Carpetani and their allies near Toletum in 193 BCE and took the town in 192 BCE. As consul he besieged and took Ambracia, ending the Aetolian War, and carried its statues to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. He was a patron of the poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ennius">Ennius</a>.</p></div>
